   "text": "Databricks Genie is free until 31 January 2027.\n\nThat's the best time to plan what it will cost.\n\nIn July, Databricks moved Genie to pay-as-you-go. A week later it paused billing for Genie One and Genie Agents until the end of January.\n\nFree tools spread fast. By the time the meter starts, usage will have grown well past what anyone planned for.\n\nHere's how I'd use the next four months:\n\n1. Measure (October)\nList every Genie space and the team behind it. Baseline who uses it and how often. Note what it answers well, and what it doesn't.\n\n2. Govern (November and December)\nGive every space a named owner. Set budgets per team: Databricks Budgets went GA in July. Agree what \"good value\" looks like before anyone argues about the invoice.\n\n3. Decide (January)\nKeep the spaces people rely on. Retire the ones nobody opens. Have alerts live before 31 January.\n\nThe State of FinOps 2026 report found 98% of FinOps teams now manage AI spend, up from 63% a year earlier. AI costs have moved from experiment to line item.\n\nThe teams that plan in the free months won't be surprised in February.\n\n#Databricks #FinOps #AI",
