   "text": "Can AI agents build your data pipelines?\n\nPART OF THEM. The honest benchmarks say which part.\n\nEveryone has seen the demo where an agent builds a pipeline in minutes. Public benchmarks give a more useful picture.\n\nOn ELT-Bench-Verified, published this March, the best agent got extract and load right 96% of the time.\n\nTransformation, the step where business logic lives, came in at 32.51%.\n\n*Moving data is nearly solved. Meaning isn't.*\n\n📦 Extract and load: use agents now. It's repetitive, checkable, and where engineers lose the most hours.\n\n🧠 Transformation: what counts as revenue, which customer is active, how two systems reconcile. Agents get it right about one time in three.\n\n🧪 dbt project tasks: the best score on the Spider 2.0-DBT leaderboard is 65.6%. Better, still not autopilot.\n\n🙋 Trust: only 33% of developers say they trust AI accuracy (Stack Overflow 2025). Healthy scepticism is the right instinct.\n\nSo split the work. AI for the repetitive, checkable steps. Fixed rules wherever results must be predictable. People own the business logic and review what ships.\n\nWhich part of your pipeline would you trust an agent with today?\n\n#DataEngineering #AI #AIAgents",
